From f4e7c485ccdfe10cc9946add7b20aedd29a8cad3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=E6=99=9A=E5=87=9DW4nN1ng?= <wn2276519232@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:47:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Add a friend footprint dashboard

Picking a friend from the new Charts tab now answers where they have been,
how often, and when. It aggregates the feed_gps rows VRCX already records
into merged visits, so hopping instances inside one world no longer reads as
a new trip, and splits out four things the raw table cannot answer directly:
the most visited worlds, a weekday by hour heat map of when they are around,
the groups they play in, and a day grouped timeline of recent trips.

Dwell time is measured from the gap between consecutive rows rather than the
stored time column, because that column resets on instance hops and only
gives a lower bound. Gaps over twelve hours are treated as VRCX having been
closed, so an offline weekend does not inflate one world, and those visits
are labelled as unknown instead of wrong.

Private rooms are kept out of the world ranking since they carry no name and
would otherwise top every list, and a profile shortcut jumps straight to that
player's footprints.
